  "observations": {
    "baseline": "Acceptance registered zero-delay retired-draft work; it fired approximately 4.1 ms later and found no live draft, before the host-consumed marker. This is not proof of a global async drain.",
    "nativeMutant": "Acceptance scheduled a new 800 ms save; its actual callback fired about 800.2 ms later and a real PUT recreated the draft during the retained observation window.",
    "lowerCandidate": "Checks no additional PUT under any id and no live session draft after 0, 799, and 1 ms, then on both sides of successive backoff-sized horizons. It observes acceptance zero-delay registration and firing. No failing request is induced here, so advancing backoff-sized horizons is not evidence that retry callbacks registered or fired. Existing retry cases own those callbacks.",
    "nativeWindow": "All original native matchers, 1500 ms observation windows, pointer contexts and mandatory build remain unchanged. The selected restored phone control does not qualify the two filtered contexts.",
    "nativeStorage": "The default 250 ms local-write timer leads to a real IndexedDB commit; later keepDeviceBranch/adoptDeviceRecord calls can trigger draft subscriptions. The unit harness storage:null cannot establish equivalence for these browser-only producers.",
    "minimum": "This mutation establishes a concrete failure detected by the retained native window. It does not establish 1500 ms as the minimum or any numerical margin; no 1500-minus-800 inference.",
    "savings": "Zero native-window reduction; additive lower test and audit evidence only."
  },
